<!--
  BlockML Core — fully qualified name value type

  FQN: org.blockml.type.FullyQualifiedName
  See docs/00_bom_core.md — Object Identity · FQN Convention
       docs/01_system.md — FQN (Fully Qualified Name)
       docs/17_type_system_bml.md — Generics · BML attribute syntax
       docs/16_framework_base_types.md — Definition Branch · ReferenceDefinition
       docs/02_mbml.md — Namespace resolution · Block Definition
-->
<block xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd"
  xmlns:btype="org.blockml.type"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.definition">

  <idea>A globally unique name referencing a Block or a definition element owned by a Block.</idea>

  <documentation>
    ValueType for fully qualified names (FQNs) — the canonical identity of every Block and
    definition element in BlockML. Unqualified name FullyQualifiedName resolves to
    org.blockml.type.FullyQualifiedName.

    FQN format (Java-style reverse-domain, dot-separated):
    • Package segments — lowercase, reverse-domain (for example org.blockml.core,
      com.machineblocks.type)
    • Class segment — PascalCase (for example Block, Integer, Wall)
    • Full form — &lt;package&gt;.&lt;ClassName&gt; (for example org.blockml.type.Integer,
      com.machineblocks.core.Block)
    Sub-Block FQNs derive as parentFqn + "." + name when omitted in source.

    Namespace prefixes in BML (core:, btype:, def:, …) map to package segments; the Namespace
    Resolver stores the resolved FQN string in BOM typeFqn fields. Unknown FQN at validate time
    → BML_UNKNOWN_TYPE.

    Generic parameters constrain which Block or definition branch a reference may target:
    • B (baseType core:Block) — owning Block branch for the referenced type
    • D (baseType core:Definition, default def:BlockDefinition) — definition element branch;
      defaults to org.blockml.definition.BlockDefinition when the second argument is omitted

    In type="..." attributes, write generic applications with round parentheses — not angle
    brackets (XML-safe, readable):
    • FullyQualifiedName(core:Block) → B = core.Block, D = def.BlockDefinition (default)
    • FullyQualifiedName(core:Block, core:Definition) → both parameters explicit
    • FullyQualifiedName(def:BlockDefinition) → B = def.BlockDefinition, D = default

    Each parenthesized argument binds one genericType parameter in declaration order (B, then D).
    With multiple parameters, the label matches the generic name and qualifies the type argument
    as a namespace prefix (abc:A → abc.A). With a single argument, only B is supplied and D
    uses defaultType. Concrete type arguments must satisfy each parameter's baseType constraint
    → BML_GENERIC_CONSTRAINT_VIOLATION.

    Primary use — meta-model and definition metadata where a type attribute holds an FQN.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <reference file="00_bom_core.md">
      Object identity and FQN convention.
    </reference>
    <reference file="01_system.md">
      FQN (Fully Qualified Name) system overview.
    </reference>
    <reference file="17_type_system_bml.md">
      Generics and BML attribute syntax for type parameters.
    </reference>
    <reference file="16_framework_base_types.md">
      Definition branch and ReferenceDefinition.
    </reference>
    <reference file="02_mbml.md">
      Namespace resolution and Block definition authoring.
    </reference>
    <reference file="12_bom_object_model.md">
      typeFqn fields in BOM structures.
    </reference>
    <reference block="org.blockml.definition.BlockDefinition">
      type and baseType attributes (Block FQN).
    </reference>
    <reference block="org.blockml.definition.PropertyDefinition">
      property type attribute (ValueType FQN).
    </reference>
    <reference block="org.blockml.definition.GenericTypeDefinition">
      parameter baseType constraint attribute.
    </reference>
    <reference block="org.blockml.definition.ContractDefinition">
      contract Block type attribute.
    </reference>
    <reference block="org.blockml.definition.ReferenceDefinition">
      cross-reference block attribute.
    </reference>
  </references>

  <genericTypes>
    <genericType name="B" baseType="core:Block" />
    <genericType name="D" baseType="core:Definition" defaultType="def:BlockDefinition" />
  </genericTypes>

  <name>FullyQualifiedName</name>
  <type>btype:FullyQualifiedName</type>
  <baseType>btype:Text</baseType>
</block>
